# Patch:        020-reshape-padding-free-sponge
# Phase:        pre
# Target:       symmetric/src/hax_reshaped.rs, symmetric/src/lib.rs, symmetric/src/sponge.rs
# Hunks:        3
# Class:        equiv-rewrite
# Gap:          docs/extractor-issues.md 23 (aeneas rejects a return that
#               leaves a nested loop).
# Cost:         none in a normal build: only the selection is behind
#               cfg(hax_backend_lean). In the extracted variant,
#               `PaddingFreeSponge::hash_iter` calls the reshaped body, which a
#               differential test equates with the original.
# Upstreamable: no: the original is the clearer code; aeneas support for
#               leaving a nested loop makes the patch unnecessary.
# Drop when:    aeneas translates `break 'outer` out of a nested loop.
# Test:         test p3-symmetric --lib hax_reshaped
# Mutation:     the reshaped body permutes once more when the input ends on a
#               block boundary, so it disagrees on the empty input and on every
#               multiple of the rate.
#
# The original absorbs a block in an inner loop and leaves both loops with `break 'outer` when the input runs dry.
# The reshaped body runs one loop over the input and keeps the rate position in a counter.
# It overwrites the same positions and calls the permutation at the same points.
#
# Tested:     test-pre-patches.py: 6715 of 6769 upstream tests pass as
#             shipped, 6715 with the pre-patches; 0 divergences from this patch.
#
diff --git a/symmetric/src/hax_reshaped.rs b/symmetric/src/hax_reshaped.rs
